00:21:38.012 --> 00:21:51.949
So for the orientation, extraversion, introversion, it's the same as when you play a card game, you get a hand of cards and you start with this one. So, but this does not mean that this is the whole game.

00:21:52.286 --> 00:22:12.405
You, of course, you play and you change and so on, but you have a certain start, starting point where you're starting from, which means that people are more inclined to an extraverted view or an introverted view just from birth. Same with the functions. He said everybody has their favorite function that came first and comes more naturally.

00:22:13.706 --> 00:22:29.227
And this is automatically the way how people will develop first with their strongest foot and strongest hand. Same way as handedness is very common. There's a certain handedness also in these functions.

00:22:30.238 --> 00:22:51.181
And he used it as an tool in his practice, but he very often just used it as an instrument to explain situations and behaviors. So he said, it's not like a patient comes to him and he tries to find out the type and then only cater to that type.

